			"notes": "Changes:\n- Redid settings system\n- Improved codebase\n- Changed command to /mhplus\n- You can now block users. Use /mhplus block <player name> to block somebody, and run it again to unblock them. You will not view messages from blocked users in lobbies or most servers.\n- MH+ now protects you from making mutable typos. If you say something like ./join abc or ad abc, your message will be blocked, but you can click the MH+ message to send it. This filter doesn't block messages like join <servername> (placeholder literal)."
		},
